Which side is opposite the $120^{\circ}$ angle?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (L) at (0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4,0);
\coordinate (T) at (-1.2,2.07846);
\draw (L)--(R)--(T)--cycle;
\draw (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=120,radius=0.55];
\path (0.48,0.83) node {$120^{\circ}$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$p$};
\path (-0.6,1.03923) node[left] {$q$};
\path (1.4,1.03923) node[above right] {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which angle is opposite the side marked $6\text{ cm}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,2.8);
\coordinate (Q) at (0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4,1);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\path (0,1.4) node[left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (P) node[above] {$P$};
\path (Q) node[below left] {$Q$};
\path (R) node[right] {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

